Package: fysetc-5inch-dsi-touch
Architecture: arm64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, linux-headers-rpi-v8, linux-headers-rpi-2712, make, kmod
Description: Touch and backlight drivers for the FYSETC 5 inch DSI Touch Screen V1.1
 Kernel drivers for the FYSETC Raspberry Pi 5 inch DSI Touch Screen MIPI LCD
 V1.1, which emulates the official Raspberry Pi 7" touchscreen:
  - fysetc_touch: touch controller (I2C 0x38), without the ghost touches of
    edt_ft5x06 and the wrong coordinates of rpi-ft5406;
  - fysetc_sleep: panel controller and backlight (I2C 0x45), so the screen
    wakes up after sleep. The backlight is on/off: brightness below 30% is off.
 .
 The modules are built on the device for every installed Raspberry Pi kernel
 and rebuilt automatically by a kernel hook when a new kernel is installed.
 .
 This package blacklists edt_ft5x06 and rpi_panel_attiny_regulator, so the
 official Raspberry Pi 7" display and other FT5x06 touchscreens will not work
 correctly while it is installed. If the modules cannot be built for a kernel
 (for example, without its headers), that kernel boots without video on the
 DSI screen.
